[{:db/id 17592186105828 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-f4d37934-3250-5bec-8382-fecffdb8f8b8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-f4d37934-3250-5bec-8382-fecffdb8f8b8" :question/id #uuid "f4d37934-3250-5bec-8382-fecffdb8f8b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-84194" :question/problem "A fair seven-sided die with sides labeled with numbers $1$ through $7$ is thrown once. If $X$ is the outcome of the die, what is the variance of $X?$" :question/worked-solution "We can compute the variance of a discrete random variable $X$ using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2}\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute the probability mass function $f(x).$ Here, there are $7$ possible outcomes ($1,2,3,4,5,6,7$) and each outcome has the same probability, so the probability mass function is as follows:\n\n| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ |\n\nNext, we compute $\\text{E}[X].$ Summing up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3)+4\\cdot f(4)+5\\cdot f(5)+6\\cdot f(6)+7\\cdot f(7) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{7})+2(\\frac{1}{7})+3(\\frac{1}{7})+4(\\frac{1}{7})+5(\\frac{1}{7})+6(\\frac{1}{7})+7(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute $\\text{E}[{X}^{2}].$ Summing up the products of each value of ${X}^{2}$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[{X}^{2}] & ={1}^{2}\\cdot f(1)+{2}^{2}\\cdot f(2)+{3}^{2}\\cdot f(3)+{4}^{2}\\cdot f(4)+{5}^{2}\\cdot f(5)+{6}^{2}\\cdot f(6)+{7}^{2}\\cdot f(7) \\\\  & =1(\\frac{1}{7})+4(\\frac{1}{7})+9(\\frac{1}{7})+16(\\frac{1}{7})+25(\\frac{1}{7})+36(\\frac{1}{7})+49(\\frac{1}{7}) \\\\  & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}]-\\text{E}[X]^{2} \\\\  & =20-{4}^{2} \\\\  & =20-16 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7a87a3d5-8e63-570a-ac6f-5e39be95722a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7a87a3d5-8e63-570a-ac6f-5e39be95722a" :answer-field/id #uuid "7a87a3d5-8e63-570a-ac6f-5e39be95722a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-87c2b1ac-f94b-5fb6-973f-99d22a68d888" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c7b86700-64fa-5575-94cc-8bcb588d9f6c" "answer-83a1e468-48a0-529c-9588-b70d4f049914" "answer-b8169a30-fe00-568f-93da-b3c870742003" "answer-87c2b1ac-f94b-5fb6-973f-99d22a68d888" "answer-8c5239c1-4a04-5072-9803-7ad54faa4a55"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c7b86700-64fa-5575-94cc-8bcb588d9f6c" :answer/id #uuid "c7b86700-64fa-5575-94cc-8bcb588d9f6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83a1e468-48a0-529c-9588-b70d4f049914" :answer/id #uuid "83a1e468-48a0-529c-9588-b70d4f049914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b8169a30-fe00-568f-93da-b3c870742003" :answer/id #uuid "b8169a30-fe00-568f-93da-b3c870742003" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-87c2b1ac-f94b-5fb6-973f-99d22a68d888" :answer/id #uuid "87c2b1ac-f94b-5fb6-973f-99d22a68d888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c5239c1-4a04-5072-9803-7ad54faa4a55" :answer/id #uuid "8c5239c1-4a04-5072-9803-7ad54faa4a55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186179988 :question/problem "Consider the affine transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=v-u,\\,y=u+v-1.\n$$\n\nLet $A$ be the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T.$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]$\n\nII. $det(A)=-2$\n\nIII. The transformation $T$ is orientation-preserving" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nLet's look at each statement in turn:\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}v-u \\\\ u+v-1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-u+v \\\\ u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Statement II is true. Computing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1=-2.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $det(A)<0,$ the affine transformation $T$ is not orientation-preserving.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186177597 :answer-field/correct 17592186177600 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083207 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-c50fb833-030a-5f7e-b663-60682ede12d9"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-c50fb833-030a-5f7e-b663-60682ede12d9" :question/id #uuid "c50fb833-030a-5f7e-b663-60682ede12d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-122392" :question/problem "The length of a curve $y=f(x)$ is given by ${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{9}{16}{e}^{6x}}\\,\\text{d}x.$ Which of the following could be  an equation for this curve?" :question/worked-solution "The arc length of a curve $y=f(x)$ between $x=a$ and $x=b$ can be found using the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\sqrt{1+[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that \n\n$$\nL={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{1+\\frac{9}{16}{e}^{6x}}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nComparing the above with the arc length formula, we see that we must have\n\n$$\n[{f}^{′}(x)]^{2}=\\frac{9}{16}{e}^{6x}\\,⟹\\,{f}^{′}(x)=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nIntegrating the above equation with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\pm \\frac{3}{4}\\int {e}^{3x}\\text{ d}x \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{1}{4}{e}^{3x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that has the required form is $y=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{3x}+4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e453f27d-3265-5a94-8683-63394b11fa22"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e453f27d-3265-5a94-8683-63394b11fa22" :answer-field/id #uuid "e453f27d-3265-5a94-8683-63394b11fa22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9316cfb5-3c9d-5c47-81ef-313e61f39c28" :answer-field/choices ["answer-cd39fea0-220a-508c-bb82-dbcfae1b08c1" "answer-42ef7e8b-dd14-5712-823d-1681f0ed2cce" "answer-9316cfb5-3c9d-5c47-81ef-313e61f39c28" "answer-3fdbcd60-3e81-5057-9137-ec0c999ae6c4" "answer-9de2dcba-6658-52b6-9531-9d55c31851da"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd39fea0-220a-508c-bb82-dbcfae1b08c1" :answer/id #uuid "cd39fea0-220a-508c-bb82-dbcfae1b08c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=4{e}^{3x}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42ef7e8b-dd14-5712-823d-1681f0ed2cce" :answer/id #uuid "42ef7e8b-dd14-5712-823d-1681f0ed2cce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{3x}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9316cfb5-3c9d-5c47-81ef-313e61f39c28" :answer/id #uuid "9316cfb5-3c9d-5c47-81ef-313e61f39c28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{3x}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3fdbcd60-3e81-5057-9137-ec0c999ae6c4" :answer/id #uuid "3fdbcd60-3e81-5057-9137-ec0c999ae6c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{1}{4}{e}^{x}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9de2dcba-6658-52b6-9531-9d55c31851da" :answer/id #uuid "9de2dcba-6658-52b6-9531-9d55c31851da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=\\frac{3}{4}{e}^{x}+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152275 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4ce39611-61f7-5873-a772-9d52755c9e24"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4ce39611-61f7-5873-a772-9d52755c9e24" :question/id #uuid "4ce39611-61f7-5873-a772-9d52755c9e24" :question/math-academy-id "q-130992" :question/problem "For the differential equation $2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy={x}^{2}-x,$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?" :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b50eac1f-2fd4-5e79-99ef-7e7a92a52cdc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b50eac1f-2fd4-5e79-99ef-7e7a92a52cdc" :answer-field/id #uuid "b50eac1f-2fd4-5e79-99ef-7e7a92a52cdc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-4ec291cf-419e-545a-91fe-9ee555957888" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4ec291cf-419e-545a-91fe-9ee555957888" "answer-ea6650bd-3f73-576d-b334-45546a281ab2" "answer-324ac1d0-643d-564f-8f08-9f84bb9e577a" "answer-3b8b705a-4bcd-52fc-b60f-645f76d62610" "answer-97cda1b8-3dc0-5b1e-87da-467116629abe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4ec291cf-419e-545a-91fe-9ee555957888" :answer/id #uuid "4ec291cf-419e-545a-91fe-9ee555957888" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ea6650bd-3f73-576d-b334-45546a281ab2" :answer/id #uuid "ea6650bd-3f73-576d-b334-45546a281ab2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-324ac1d0-643d-564f-8f08-9f84bb9e577a" :answer/id #uuid "324ac1d0-643d-564f-8f08-9f84bb9e577a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b8b705a-4bcd-52fc-b60f-645f76d62610" :answer/id #uuid "3b8b705a-4bcd-52fc-b60f-645f76d62610" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{x}{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+y=x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-97cda1b8-3dc0-5b1e-87da-467116629abe" :answer/id #uuid "97cda1b8-3dc0-5b1e-87da-467116629abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+\\frac{1}{x-1}y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186184160 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-de50db69-1f49-5b62-bb8f-7cba652094a4"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-de50db69-1f49-5b62-bb8f-7cba652094a4" :question/id #uuid "de50db69-1f49-5b62-bb8f-7cba652094a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-130663" :question/problem "If $A=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]$, then ${A}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${A}^{2}=A,$ so $A$ is an idempotent matrix. \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${A}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{4} & ={A}^{2}\\cdot {A}^{2} \\\\  & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & ={A}^{2} \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{A}^{4}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e2b3e7c5-52c2-5e4b-bcbf-08cf2d113f06"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e2b3e7c5-52c2-5e4b-bcbf-08cf2d113f06" :answer-field/id #uuid "e2b3e7c5-52c2-5e4b-bcbf-08cf2d113f06" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-79b811ba-d237-5358-9a7b-e5099ee68347" :answer-field/choices ["answer-6988567e-c6b3-5730-a2d4-b0c476a8c21a" "answer-02156f42-01b9-5208-be76-46dd56d1f051" "answer-fb87aec8-67bb-5868-9fd5-615026521a6f" "answer-c40a1344-3c43-5a5d-97e2-770817ab45f0" "answer-79b811ba-d237-5358-9a7b-e5099ee68347"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6988567e-c6b3-5730-a2d4-b0c476a8c21a" :answer/id #uuid "6988567e-c6b3-5730-a2d4-b0c476a8c21a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-02156f42-01b9-5208-be76-46dd56d1f051" :answer/id #uuid "02156f42-01b9-5208-be76-46dd56d1f051" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fb87aec8-67bb-5868-9fd5-615026521a6f" :answer/id #uuid "fb87aec8-67bb-5868-9fd5-615026521a6f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c40a1344-3c43-5a5d-97e2-770817ab45f0" :answer/id #uuid "c40a1344-3c43-5a5d-97e2-770817ab45f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-79b811ba-d237-5358-9a7b-e5099ee68347" :answer/id #uuid "79b811ba-d237-5358-9a7b-e5099ee68347" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-b54594b5-9269-55c1-947a-7f5c52c7cdb8" :activity/id #uuid "b54594b5-9269-55c1-947a-7f5c52c7cdb8" :activity/title "Quiz 9" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046659 :activity/steps ["step-cea1f50c-f411-5b8e-8725-9f1453039640" "step-de23c22a-cee1-55c5-9cbb-8003a72fc391" "step-8ec26814-7bcf-59e5-88c6-511a1ee3466e" "step-4d26866c-abaf-5108-9657-988713fa86d0" "step-2e680767-2f69-5742-9e88-d83d12508574" "step-68027ec1-b3e8-5d56-9340-a76e6e272009" "step-4be5d573-c74c-5d15-84dc-67c9e32a69b2"] :activity/first-step "step-cea1f50c-f411-5b8e-8725-9f1453039640" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-cea1f50c-f411-5b8e-8725-9f1453039640" :step/id #uuid "cea1f50c-f411-5b8e-8725-9f1453039640" :step/content "question-f4d37934-3250-5bec-8382-fecffdb8f8b8" :step/next "step-de23c22a-cee1-55c5-9cbb-8003a72fc391" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-de23c22a-cee1-55c5-9cbb-8003a72fc391" :step/id #uuid "de23c22a-cee1-55c5-9cbb-8003a72fc391" :step/content 17592186125217 :step/next "step-8ec26814-7bcf-59e5-88c6-511a1ee3466e" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-8ec26814-7bcf-59e5-88c6-511a1ee3466e" :step/id #uuid "8ec26814-7bcf-59e5-88c6-511a1ee3466e" :step/content 17592186436028 :step/next "step-4d26866c-abaf-5108-9657-988713fa86d0" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-4d26866c-abaf-5108-9657-988713fa86d0" :step/id #uuid "4d26866c-abaf-5108-9657-988713fa86d0" :step/content 17592186179988 :step/next "step-2e680767-2f69-5742-9e88-d83d12508574" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2e680767-2f69-5742-9e88-d83d12508574" :step/id #uuid "2e680767-2f69-5742-9